  "plain": "In the 1970s, a man named Pat Price is said to have used remote viewing, a claimed practice of describing distant places with the mind alone, to read a file inside \"a top CIA security facility\" in the United States. A guest named Dan Sheehan tells Michels this from the reports that the remote viewer Ingo Swann wrote for the Guardian's Office, an office of the Church of Scientology, and he also names the researcher Russell Targ. If true, the CIA's own secrets were open to the people it was testing."
